# SHARED GitHub Actions VARIABLES — the house rules every repo calling the
# shared workflows gets. Non-sensitive; committed; published with the package.
#
# A repo adds or overrides any key in its own .github/actions.env; the repo's
# value wins. Keep here only what is genuinely the same everywhere — anything
# tied to one project (AUTO_PROJECT_NUMBER, AUTO_MILESTONE_TITLE, deploy
# settings) belongs to that repo.
#
# Read at run time, never copied onto repos: the actions load this file from the
# copy of ebalzan/ci the runner downloads for `uses: …@v4`
# (scripts/shared-vars.mjs) and fill every key the repo leaves unset. A change
# here reaches the repos when it is released and the major tag moves to it — no
# bootstrap run.
#
# Only values that differ from the code defaults live here
# (actions/auto-pr/action.yml, actions/work-pr/rules.mjs): the board owner is the
# repo owner, a PR over 500 changed lines gets a warning
# (AUTO_MAX_CHANGED_LINES), and there is no board or milestone unless the repo
# sets one. The workflows pass the repo's variables whole (REPO_VARS_JSON), so
# setting a key here or in a repo is all it takes — no workflow edit.
#
# Full key reference: docs/CONFIGURATION.md.

# Claude model that writes the PR descriptions (actions/auto-pr, through Claude
# Code). Kept here, not just as the code default, so it can be switched without
# a code change. AUTO_DESCRIBE_EFFORT: low | medium | high | xhigh | max —
# ignored for Haiku, which does not accept it.
AUTO_DESCRIBE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
AUTO_DESCRIBE_EFFORT=low
